#. Tag: title
#: app-files.docbook:13 app-files.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration Files Used by &kdevelop;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: app-files.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; uses a series of configuration files which are distributed "
"amongst several directories. There are two main groups of configuration "
"files to distinguish:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: app-files.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"app-files-default\">&kdevelop; Default Configuration</link> "
"&mdash; files set up when &kdevelop; was installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: app-files.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"app-files-user\">User Oriented Configuration</link> &mdash; "
"files which contain user modifications of the defaults as well as settings "
"made by the &kdevelop; application itself and its plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: app-files.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kdevelop; Default Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: app-files.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On installation, &kdevelop; writes some default information files for setup "
"and configuration purposes into subdirectories of the <filename class="
"\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar></filename> installation directory "
"(usually something like <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde</filename>, "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr/local/kde</filename>, or some other user-"
"defined installation directory, see <link linkend=\"kdevelop-install"
"\">Installing &kdevelop;</link>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: app-files.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default &kdevelop; Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: app-files.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is only one &kdevelop; specific default configuration file in the "
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config/</"
"filename> directory:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: app-files.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "kdeveloprc"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: app-files.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This file contains the basic settings &kdevelop; needs to start. It will be "
"copied to the user's <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/"
"share/config</filename> directory when &kdevelop; does not find a "
"<filename>kdeveloprc</filename> file there on startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: app-files.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "Application Specific Defaults"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: app-files.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most &kdevelop; features are provided by KParts. These are basically "
"applications specially designed to run in the &kdevelop; framework (see the "
"overview in the <link linkend=\"plugin-tools\">Plugin Tools</link> "
"appendix). Each KPart application has its own set of configuration files "
"whose defaults will be stored in several subdirectories of the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/apps/</filename> "
"installation directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: app-files.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are quite a lot of default configuration subdirectories in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/apps/</filename> whose "
"names all start with a <filename>kdev</filename> sequence. Most of them are "
"for &kdevelop; internal use only. They might be deliberately grouped for "
"readability as:"
msgstr ""

